=3D"-1" data-testid=3D"expandable-text-box">I clicked on Slack's new AI age=
nt this week.

You know what it can do? Join channels. Send messages. Upload files.
That's it. That's the agent.

No business context. No customer intelligence. No understanding of what you=
r company actually does.

This is what happens when "ship it" beats "make it work."

Every enterprise vendor is racing to say they have AI agents. Most of them =
are just bots from 2018 with a new label. And here's the part nobody wants =
to say out loud =E2=80=94 they're not just useless. They're liabilities.

An agent that doesn't understand your business will hallucinate at scale. I=
t will erode customer trust faster than any human ever could. And it will t=
each an entire generation of buyers that "AI agent" means "thing that doesn=
't work."

Meanwhile, look at what Anthropic did with Claude. They didn't ship agents =
until the foundation was ready. Reasoning first. Context first. Capability =
before marketing.

That's the discipline most companies don't have.

The real question isn't "do you have agents." It's: what does your agent kn=
ow about your business that it didn't know yesterday?

If the answer is nothing, you bought a press release =E2=80=94 not a produc=
t.
